{"name":"Gondolier","hex":"#5db1c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gondolier","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boatperson who propels a gondola, especially in Venice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gondolier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gondolier (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Gondolier\" is a song by the French singer Dalida, first released on an EP in December 1957. It was her second major hit after \"Bambino\". Reaching No. 1 on both the La Bourse des Chansons chart and the Music Hall chart in France, it was the title song for Dalida's 1958 album Gondolier. The song also reached No. 1 on the Belgian and Canadian charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Gondolier_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondolier_(song)","wikidata":"Q5581470"},{"title":"Gondola","blocks":[{"text":"The gondola is a traditional, flat-bottomed Venetian rowing boat, well suited to the conditions of the Venetian lagoon in Italy. It is typically propelled by a gondolier, who uses a rowing oar, which is not fastened to the hull, in a sculling manner, and also acts as the rudder. The uniqueness of the gondola includes its being asymmetrical along the length, making the single-oar propulsion more efficient."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Gondola_Ride.jpg/330px-Gondola_Ride.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gondola","wikidata":"Q182916"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Brooklyn_Museum_-_La_Riva_-_John_Singer_Sargent.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_La_Riva_-_John_Singer_Sargent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Brooklyn_Museum_-_La_Riva_-_John_Sing